Third-party components added for plugins, routines, and agent handoff
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Model Context Protocol Kotlin SDK
  io.modelcontextprotocol:kotlin-sdk-client 0.15.0
  https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/kotlin-sdk
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Used for Streamable HTTP and SSE MCP sessions, tool listing, and tool calls.
  JSON-RPC framing is the SDK's. This app does not ship a second JSON-RPC client.

AppAuth for Android
  net.openid:appauth 0.11.1
  https://github.com/openid/AppAuth-Android
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Used to open the authorization request and exchange the authorization code
  for MCP plugin sign-in. Protected-resource metadata (RFC 9728) and dynamic
  client registration (RFC 7591) stay in this app because AppAuth does not
  implement them.

JetBrains Koog
  https://github.com/JetBrains/koog
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Considered for the agent loop and scheduled routines. Not bundled.
  The app already has an agent loop (provider adapters, compaction, and tool
  traces). Replacing it would duplicate that work. Routines are scheduled with
  AndroidX WorkManager, which is already a dependency, because Koog does not
  provide an Android scheduler.

